    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/12082/original/Roeland_Flyer_DNL.png?1680531746",
    "bio": "My name is Roeland Krijnen. I have been working in the Netherlands again since 2017 after having lived abroad (Aruba) for about fifteen years where I had my own health practices and worked as a physiotherapist for the Olympic Committee for a while. For example, I traveled to The Pan American Games. In addition, I gave plenty of workshops and trainings in the field of health and disease prevention to companies and major hotels. If I may briefly describe my life path here, I mainly encounter human interest upon closer inspection. I am very interested in (human) life and over time have consciously started to explore many aspects that are 'obvious': health, its philosophical depth, environment, living conditions, culture, (changing) life goals, place in the world, the variety of spirituality and meaning, and of course our limitations and errors. I follow both the scientific paths and the empirical there-is-no-academic-proof paths. I find it quite amusing that both paths can explain the seemingly strange but brilliant principles of yin-yang. By working with people of various nationalities and conditions: from top-fit marines to cautious elderly; from people with a difficult knee inflammation to terminal cancer patients; from vulnerable children to high-level athletes, I draw from a wealth of countless encounters. Which I like to use to come up with solutions, of course.",
