    "bio": "My name is Marianne Verbeek. During a long stay in China in 1988, I first got acquainted with Tai Qi and Traditional Chinese Medicine. After that, I followed lessons for years with Dr. Shen (Eastern and Western doctor) and Shen Jin, with whom I completed the international training programs to become a Buqi Therapist and Professional Taijiwuxigong Teacher. The acupuncture and herbal medicine training followed thereafter. Characteristic of my approach is an attentive, spacious approach combined with broad paramedical experience. Always seeking simplicity, playfulness, and beauty in the everyday, concrete, and ever-changing moment that encompasses everything! I enjoy treating complex support requests, such as chronic fatigue, oncology, Parkinson's, all kinds of pain, palliative care, elderly and relaxation issues, and aim to find a suitable answer for each support request. I am BIG-registered.",
