    "bio": "It's been more than twenty years since I became familiar with Eastern philosophy. This meant a source of recognition, everything about this vision of life made sense to me. Eastern philosophy is not book knowledge. During my acupuncture training and the years of practical experience that followed, this philosophy of life has gradually enriched and deepened for me. Only by putting it into practice and experiencing it can it provide clarity in a natural way. Both in my own life and in the treatment of clients. I completed my acupuncture training in 2009 at the Qing Bai academy. Followed by various further training in the Netherlands and abroad by Dr. Richard Teh-Fu Tan and his Balance Method. In the years that followed, I got to know the psycho-somatic approach of acupuncture better and facilitating clients in Self-healing and finding inner peace has played a major role in the treatments. My gift of sensing what a client needs help with has developed over the years. In a natural presence, I can intuitively feel at a deep level what is possible in an acupuncture treatment at that moment to relieve a complaint. Mental and emotional complaints can almost always be traced back to a certain clouding and confusion about how we experience ourselves. Therefore, it is beautiful moments when I see a client brighten up during a treatment, often in wonder about how it happened.",
