    "bio": "Hello, my name is Evelien Smid. I live freely outside with my family and work there with a lot of love in the garden. Furthermore, I love learning or creating new things. With great pleasure, I work in my acupuncture practice in Wagenborgen. I love the contact with the other, to look together at where the bottlenecks are. Me from the acupuncture and you as a connoisseur of your body and your life. The treatment is aimed at feeling better, gaining insight, and feeling what is and isn't good/handy. Stimulating the body to come more into balance. And every time I am amazed again by the enormous, subtle power of acupuncture. In addition to general acupuncture, I have specialized in pediatric acupuncture, women's health, the relationship between body and mind, and guiding people in an oncological trajectory. Think, for example, of reducing the side effects of chemotherapy. Furthermore, I practice a form of Japanese acupuncture, Toyohari. That style is very subtle, completely painless, and people experience it as very pleasant. But most of all, I am interested in health and every unique person. Feel welcome.",
