    "bio": "Connection in life is what is reflected in acupuncture for me. One cannot exist without the other, just like yin and yang cannot exist separately. The holistic view of the human being and their environment. As an acupuncturist, I try to support people in restoring a disturbed balance in their energy and accessing their self-healing ability. In addition to my work as an acupuncturist, I work with animals. Then I am in the present. They are and are beautiful in that. Without judgment, they make contact. This is what I find important as an acupuncturist. Listening to the client, being able to understand this unique person with the question they bring. Trying to do this without judgment. Breathing is a focal point during the treatment. Breath, so inseparably connected to life energy.",
