    "bio": "Acupuncture Erp, Annita Poorthuis Acupuncture is no longer just common in China, but in the Netherlands as well, traditional general practitioners and specialists are using acupuncture more often as a complement to treatments. Over the past 20 years, I have seen acupuncture rapidly gaining popularity, which is evident in the number of referrals from general practitioners and specialists. Rheumatologists regularly refer clients for pain complaints, ENT doctors for tinnitus, and at the smoking cessation clinic, there are also brochures from my practice. In addition to years of practical experience, I have completed internships in China (Beijing and Shanghai) and with Prof. Dr. Cheng Qian. My focus areas are hay fever, skin complaints, and postoperative complaints. Do you have any questions about your complaints? Feel free to contact me. Annita Poorthuis, working in Erp, Uden, and Enschede",
