    "bio": "My name is Zhihong Wan. I was born in China. Since 2009, I have been living in the Netherlands and I have followed a bachelor's degree program at Hogeschool Rotterdam. Through a fortunate coincidence, I came into contact with acupuncture. Subsequently, Traditional Chinese Medicine crossed my path and I was drawn to it. After four years of study, I successfully completed the acupuncture program at the TCM (Traditional Chinese Medicine), Shenzhou University in Amsterdam. In addition to the acupuncture program, I have also successfully completed the basic medical knowledge program. For years, I worked at a well-known acupuncture practice in The Hague. There, I gained a vast amount of experience in TCM treatments. Because I am naturally persistent, I will always strive to find the therapy that suits you best. I have high standards for quality, am very precise, and regularly attend refresher courses. This allows me to stay informed about the latest developments and techniques in the field of acupuncture. Furthermore, I visit China at least once a year for further study, to improve my technique and expand my specialized knowledge of acupuncture. This enables me to offer patients even more effective treatments.",
