    "bio": "My name is Mirjam Persons. I have been searching for a long time for a profession that really suits me. Initially, I studied occupational therapy and worked as an occupational therapist in a nursing home for fourteen years. It was nice, but something was missing. I kept hearing more and more about acupuncture and noticed that it sparked my interest. Eventually, I decided to pursue the training, and that was it! Suddenly, I was a very motivated student. That was not like me at all. ;-) I read all the books that were part of the training, including the English ones! Instead of getting passing grades, I was now getting eights and nines. I notice that the knowledge I have now with acupuncture enriches my perspective on conditions, limitations, diseases, and health. I now work entirely in my own acupuncture practice and I am very happy with that. I feel completely at home and have found my profession!",
