    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/12536/original/foto_E_Wijga.JPG?1680531824",
    "bio": "Nice to meet you, I am Esther Wijga, I have been working as an acupuncturist since 2011 and my practice is located in Aalsmeer. After a long search for a solution to my allergies, I came into contact with acupuncture. This was a revelation for me, acupuncture relieved me of most chronic ailments. This made me very enthusiastic and that's why I started the four-year acupuncture training at the Qing-Bai Academy for Chinese Medicine. Acupuncture has truly become my passion and it is wonderful to be able to help so many other people. In 2009, our family traveled through Thailand for a few months. During this trip, I took a Thai massage course at the WATPO Thai Traditional Medical School in Bangkok. That's where my passion for massage originated, which is why I later started the Qigong Tuina training. I completed this two-year training in 2019. I find Qigong Tuina massage to be a very effective addition to acupuncture treatments and I use it frequently. In 2010, I graduated as an acupuncturist, but I find it important to continue to develop myself and broaden and deepen my knowledge. That's why I regularly attend courses and training in the fields of acupuncture, nutrition, healing, and spirituality. Currently, I am taking a course in intuitive development and mediumship. Over the years, I have already been able to help many people and reduce or completely eliminate their complaints with acupuncture. Are you brave enough to undergo treatment with me?",
