    "bio": "My name is Jeanette Donselaar. I have been working as a nurse specializing in Intensive Care since I was 17. I have always been involved in Western medicine. Until the moment my late husband was bent over in pain and went to the acupuncturist, only to come back home walking upright. I needed to know more about it. I then went to the open day of TCMA (Traditional Chinese Medicine Academy Netherlands) and was completely enthusiastic. I enrolled and the 3-year study turned out to be a huge enrichment. Meanwhile, I have expanded my knowledge and continue to expand it further on Auriculotherapy/ear acupuncture. I am very drawn to this treatment method because you can treat the entire body through the ear. This method of treatment works very well alongside traditional acupuncture. In addition to the holistic treatment that acupuncture entails, I am still a nurse. No longer in Intensive Care, but as a Travel Nurse. I now provide travel advice and vaccinations to travelers. But working according to Chinese Medicine, the holistic approach to addressing the complaint(s), is where my passion lies.",
