    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/12381/original/1_%283%29.jpg?1680531795",
    "bio": "My name is Marwytske Sprong-Venema. I am a physiotherapist and have also been working in the hospital for more than 25 years. As a caregiver, I often face the question of why one person recovers more difficultly than another. And why some complaints do not improve. I wanted an explanation for people with unexplained, long-term, or vague complaints or complaints for which Western medicine has no solution. I obtained my diploma in Classical Acupuncture at the Academy for Chinese Medicine 'Qing-Bai' in Amersfoort in 2015. This training has given me a different perspective on disease and health. The theory and application of Chinese medicine have proven to be of so much value to me that I decided to start my own practice! Auricular acupuncture is a beautiful addition to the Classical Acupuncture treatment that I use. The Oncological Acupuncture training I have completed allows me to guide patients in every stage of cancer treatment. Acupuncture can also provide relief to patients with chronic complaints who are not undergoing active cancer treatment.",
