    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/11849/original/Acupunctuur_Suwen_-_portret.jpg?1680531697",
    "bio": "My name is Swen Dudek. My fascination with Eastern culture began with wushu and later tai chi and qi gong. Previously active as a visual artist and musician, a new passion was born after a guasha course. This was the start of my three-year study to become a tuina therapist at the Shenmen Institute in Düsseldorf. After a one-year detour for basic medical knowledge, I successfully completed my three-year acupuncture studies at TCMA Amsterdam in 2018. This fascinating profession, in which you never stop learning, draws from a history of more than four thousand years. Body and mind are one, everything is constantly in motion, both in nature and in humans. Acupuncture stimulates and restores the self-healing ability and balance. Everything is interconnected and ultimately traceable back to a certain energetic state. I want to be consciously present for you in the moment, without judgment, because every moment is an opportunity for change.",
