    "bio": "It all starts with attention. In my practice, there is time and attention to tell your story. And there is a half-hour intake interview. More information means more extensive and better filtering of what is important and how I will treat your complaints. People find this pleasant. To have the time. Regardless of whether the cause of the complaints is more psychological, more emotional, or more physical in nature; it is about the pathological/physiological combination. And as an acupuncturist, you treat holistically. A powerful additional tool alongside body acupuncture is ear acupuncture, where the mental-emotional part is approached extra. And brain processes are better controlled. Some of my patients want and receive this form of acupuncture in addition, because of the broad well-being effect. Started as a physiotherapist, continued with Shiatsu, through this Japanese treatment method followed the Chinese and became an Acupuncturist [since 2006]. The knowledge of the human body was welcome in the work as an acupuncturist. Results count and what I get in return is gratitude and satisfaction. Satisfaction in the profession, so that counts. Good Qi wished! Roy Pronk",
