    "bio": "Actually, I did not choose acupuncture. It came my way! I was a physiotherapist, got rheumatism and was declared unfit in 1994. To recover myself, I started The Art of Life training at the Kushi Institute. There I was treated with acupuncture. To my surprise, after three weeks I felt like a different person! I was so enthusiastic that in 2003 I started studying acupuncture at Qing Bai. Since 2007 I have had my acupuncture practice. To work even more subtly, I started studying Japanese Acupuncture, Toyohari in 2009. Through the different trainings, you can play with what is best to use for each patient, each treatment. My affinity lies particularly with rheumatism, women's complaints, allergies, stress, and depression.",
