    "bio": "My name is Marina van Kuilenburg. Since 2009 I have been working as an acupuncturist and tuina therapist. I followed the training at the Academy for Chinese Medicine Qing Bai. At the age of 18, I started the training to become a radiologic technologist. I still do this work (part-time) with a lot of pleasure. Over the years, I increasingly disliked the fact that there was no longer time for just a chat with or attention to the patient during work in healthcare. When I came into contact with acupuncture, I found it so interesting and special that I decided to follow the training and set up a practice. I regularly attend further training courses to keep my knowledge and skills up to date. For example, I have taken courses on Dr. Tan's balance method, gynecology, pain management, ear acupuncture, and Chinese herbs. In my practice, I find the holistic approach and taking time for my clients very important. Together with the client, I try to find a way to bring both body and mind as much as possible into balance.",
