    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/12087/original/AAKU-Els-Kuin-Home-4.jpg?1731707530",
    "bio": "I have been combining Western and Eastern medicine since completing my TCM training in 2016. This offers good effects for conditions such as sleep problems, burnout, hay fever, gastrointestinal disorders, and pain, where Western medicine does not provide a sufficient solution. As a physician, I have long experienced that as a human being, you have a great self-healing ability. Although I am involved and empathetic, I also try to make myself redundant in your life as quickly as possible. I hear what you say, listen between the lines, and extract what is essential to address the complaints. Sometimes the source is different complaints than what you initially came for. By actively implementing the advice given, we work together thoroughly on your recovery, leading to quick results. Therefore, in my work, I strive for you to be able to move forward after the treatments. To know how to get your life back on track and how to maintain it. To enjoy the things you do again and have time for them. To have balance and be able to make conscious choices that suit you and your life. And above all, to prevent new complaints. Specializations: in sports, in Chinese skull acupuncture (Jason Hao), and Japanese skull acupuncture Yamamoto. Skull acupuncture helps with the consequences of a severe concussion, recovery of functioning after a stroke, and pain treatment. Other areas of focus are sleep problems, burnout, stress, allergies, menopausal symptoms, menstrual complaints, and sports medicine.",
