    "bio": "Nothing comes for free, a cliché or not?! After the birth of my first child, the struggle to shed the last pregnancy kilos has brought an awareness of the importance of nutrition, exercise, and balance between body and mind. But more importantly, it has stirred something within me. The quest for well-being could begin. Along the way, I have been trained in various massage techniques. Through these interests, I have come into contact with Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) and in particular acupuncture. A new world has opened up for me. A world where it is not the complaint but the person that is central. The person as a whole, as a unique individual. I have successfully (and with great pleasure) completed the 3-year study of Traditional Chinese Medicine as well as a basic Western medical education. I enjoyed both courses at the Qing Bai Academy before starting as an independent acupuncturist. Driven by my passion, I regularly attend further training courses to deepen my knowledge and stay informed of the latest developments. My children are (almost) grown up now, and I enjoy the beautiful and small things in life. I like to immerse myself in the beauty of nature in our wonderful Netherlands during long walks. In my creative moods, I paint, and music, alongside acupuncture, is my great passion. I have learned that enjoying life is so important, especially to cope with the difficult moments in our lives.",
