    "bio": "My name is Maya Lentze. Raised with a holistic lifestyle, where healthy nutrition, exercise, and nature were paramount. As a child, I already visited the acupuncturist, who were still scarce at that time! In 1989 I obtained my physiotherapy diploma and worked for several years in various physiotherapy practices in Zeeland. However, I increasingly noticed that the human image used in physiotherapy at that time was too limited for me. After working in the rehabilitation industry for a few years, I completed a basic training in Chinese medicine and a professional training in classical acupuncture (Qing Bai). I then completed additional acupuncture training in Belgium (Jing Ming) recognized by the NVA (Dutch Acupuncture Association). The many additional courses and further training I have taken over the years allow me to apply a wide range of techniques from Chinese medicine to various complaints and conditions.",
