    "bio": "I was born and raised in China, where I discovered my interest in Traditional Chinese Medicine. In 2010, I moved to the Netherlands for love, and here my passion for acupuncture further developed. I completed the four-year professional training for Traditional Chinese Medicine and Western Medical Basic Knowledge (CPION/SHO) in three years at the Qing Bai Academy in Amersfoort. My motivation is to help and support people. During and after the training, I already helped one day a week at AWB - Acupuncturists Without Borders - at the open practice locations: de Rijp, Heiloo, Hoorn, Bergen, Petten, to help refugees from different countries (including Ukraine, Syria, and various African countries). I treated refugees with post-traumatic stress, pain, and other conditions. Among them were also many children who had fled with their parents. From this, I derive a lot of satisfaction: 'I want to be there for people when they need it'.",
