    "bio": "In 2004, I first came into contact with acupuncture during a conversation I had with the then-director of Qing Bai. This sparked my interest/curiosity in acupuncture. In early 2019, I experienced the power of acupuncture myself after a burnout. The acupuncture treatments brought me back to myself completely. In 2020, I started the 3.5-year training to become an acupuncturist, which I completed in 2024. It fascinates me daily what the needling of acupuncture points has for a beneficial, calming effect on body & mind. Chinese Acupuncture is a holistic healing method and aims to restore balance in the entire body in a natural way, reducing or even eliminating your health problems.",
