    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/13058/original/foto_mw._Yang.jpg?1680531917",
    "bio": "I am Lihua and I work with great pleasure as an acupuncturist. I have many years of experience with Traditional Chinese Medicine. I respect classical Chinese medicine so I follow the classical prescriptions for all my treatments. I have been appointed as a board member of the world TCM Forum. I am a disciple of Chen Yunhe, the heir of the intangible Tai Su pulse Chakra method. I am a 49th generation heir of the Medicine King clan. I started studying Traditional Chinese Medicine because I had acute hepatitis A when I was five years old and the hospital had given up on my treatment. An old Chinese doctor gave me three prescriptions and my mother gave me one prescription to take and I was cured. The second reason was that my mother had lymphatic tuberculosis when I was a baby and the hospital had given up on treating my mother. It was Traditional Chinese Medicine that saved both of us. So later when I grew up, I studied Chinese medicine with my godfather. I hope that what I have learned can be used to help more people, to relieve them of their ailments and pain. 2018: Diploma Herbal Medicine obtained, Shenzhou Open University of TCM 2019: Diploma Foundations of Western Medicine obtained, Shenzhou Open University of TCM 2019: Diploma Foundations of Chinese Medicine obtained, Shenzhou Open University of TCM 2021: Diploma Acupuncture obtained, Shenzhou Open University of TCM",
