    "bio": "My name is Kitty/ Xinghua Bao. From a young age, I grew up with Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM). We didn't have medicines at home but used natural herbs when my brother or sister had a wound or were sick. We ate very healthily, with lots of fresh vegetables, and played and worked a lot outside. Even as a child, I knew that I wanted to take care of people, make them better and healthier. I studied in China with a well-known family of doctors where the knowledge of TCM had been passed down through many generations. I also gained extensive work experience in China. In my practice in the Netherlands, I have already been able to heal various people from conditions such as muscle pain, hernia, rheumatism, gallbladder inflammation, stress, bowel problems, and many others. Now that I am a proud mother of a son, children's health has become even more important, and I always integrate traditional treatments with dietary and lifestyle advice in my approach. Helping people and making them better is what I love to do most, and I hope to be able to help you in the future as well. You are very welcome in my practice.",
