    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/11672/original/c7560245-0abd-46df-97ef-2e5d09cfd1e8.jpeg?1765898096",
    "bio": "Background My name is Caroline Albers. As a twenty-something, I came into contact with acupuncture. Time and time again, I was amazed by the beneficial and spectacular effects of the therapy and became intrigued by the Chinese medicine and philosophy that underlie it: ancient knowledge of humans and nature that is still surprisingly relevant. And that enables the body to solve problems on its own. A natural approach without side effects. The beauty is that you can endlessly delve into acupuncture and always discover new things. And because I prefer to work where people are at the center, I decided to pursue acupuncture training. I completed the bachelor's degree in classical acupuncture at the Academy for Chinese Medicine Qing-Bai. After that, I attended various postgraduate courses to maintain and further develop my practical and theoretical skills. I took courses in pain treatment, ear acupuncture, gynecology, nutrition, and cosmetic acupuncture. In my practice in Amstelveen, I work together with two acupuncturists/physiotherapists and we share knowledge and experience daily. Specialization My affinity lies with complaints that many women face throughout their lives: hormonal complaints, weight problems, stress and insomnia, fatigue, and skin aging. In addition to acupuncture treatment, I provide supportive information in the form of booklets and flyers. FemVitaal Attention, a calming atmosphere, and a substantive approach are the keywords that I associate with my practice FemVitaal. It is a place where women are at the center and where you receive all the time and attention you need. With the aim of making you feel fit and energetic again quickly.",
