    "bio": "After 15 years of working in youth care and as our children grew older, I felt the need to start studying again. I then studied phytotherapy (herbal medicine) for a number of years and now regularly make custom creams, ointments, and soaps for people with skin conditions such as eczema, psoriasis, and sun allergy, as well as a facial cream for those who love a pure product. Through a classmate, I ended up at an open day of Qing-Bai, the academy for Chinese medicine. There I was captivated by the holistic view of people's complaints. Body and mind cannot be separated. Emotions can lead to physical complaints and vice versa. I find it important to address the cause instead of just treating the symptoms. This way, complaints can be permanently resolved. Acupuncture also addresses the underlying causes and treats the person as a whole. Balance is the magic word. What really appeals to me is that each treatment is uniquely tailored to the individual. If 3 people come with the same complaint, the cause can be different three times, leading to unique treatments. Since obtaining my diploma, I have regularly attended further training courses, both in the field of Western and Eastern medicine, to continue developing myself professionally and personally. This way, I can serve you better and play a role in improving quality of life.",
