    "languages": "Not listed",
    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/12497/original/4.jpg?1680531816",
    "bio": "My name is Nusret Vlashi. As you undoubtedly know and experience in your daily life, pain management remains a delicate matter, especially since the healing process, especially in chronic conditions, can be extremely difficult. Unfortunately, analgesics (painkillers) are not always sufficient! Trained and educated in medicine in Kosovo, skepticism has become my second nature. It took me a while to actually become convinced of Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM). Now I know it as an extremely effective and completely harmless form of pain management and anti-inflammatory. It is my firm belief that pain and pain management are very personal and should be approached in that way. The general principle used in TCM to explain the phenomenon of 'pain' is: 'if there is free flow, there is no pain, but if there is blockage, there is pain.' This statement applies to all types of pain, regardless of the cause. It is the subjective experience of a lack of flow of qi and xue. It is my ambition to reach as many people as possible and relieve their pain, or at least alleviate it, using this therapy in combination with my knowledge and experience in the medical field.",
