    "bio": "After completing my physiotherapy education, I worked for several years in a private physiotherapy practice. Because I had complaints about an eye and did not make any progress in conventional medicine, I ended up at an acupuncturist. With acupuncture, my complaint disappeared like snow in the sun. During my treatment, I received a good logical explanation of where my complaint came from. That's where my interest in Traditional Chinese Medicine began. For years now, I have been complementing my physiotherapy treatments with acupuncture treatments with a lot of passion, or I treat only with acupuncture and, if necessary, with Chinese herbs. I see a lot of muscle and joint complaints, but also headaches, burnout complaints, menopausal complaints, and unexplained complaints. People who have been everywhere but whose complaint does not go away. Solving a difficult puzzle of complaints is what I love to do. Supplemented with nutrition and lifestyle tips. Health is my passion and my hobby, I am always busy with it and continue to develop myself through courses and self-study. I would like to share this passion with you. I work at Jordens Fysio Medisch Centrum where many disciplines in healthcare are present, both Western medical and alternative. Together we try to find the best treatment for your complaint.",
