    "focus": "Acupuncture, Acupressure, Cupping, Moxa, Ear Acupuncture, Chinese Herbs, Chinese Nutrition, Electro-acupuncture, Oncologie",
    "experience": "Not listed",
    "languages": "Not listed",
    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/11941/original/Profielfoto_Marja.jpg?1680531718",
    "bio": "My name is Marja Hamelijnck and I work as an acupuncturist, herbalist, and physiotherapist in my home practice (since 2007). It is my mission to help clients rebalance. Whether they are seriously ill, have complaints, or just need a little support. As long as I can remember, I wanted to become a doctor 'later' and help people with their health. Early on, I realized that I did not want to do this by prescribing medication but that I wanted to contribute to people's self-healing ability. After studying physiotherapy, I worked for twelve years as a physiotherapist in a private practice. In my work, I noticed that complaints are rarely purely physical and that the psyche also plays a major role in having complaints. I found that I was reaching the limits of my profession and decided to study Traditional Chinese Medicine. In this approach, disease is seen as an imbalance, both on a physical and psychological and emotional level. In my opinion, by utilizing the qualities of both Western and Eastern medicine, you can provide the best holistic treatment to people who are ill or have complaints. I would like to bridge the gap between conventional and complementary medicine so that we can choose what is most beneficial for each individual.",
