    "bio": "My name is Petra Lambert. Since I was eleven, I received acupuncture and accompanied other patients. This unconscious practical training continued until the death of my teacher/acupuncturist (also a physiotherapist). He was already trained in Taiwan in the late sixties, early seventies. After high school, I studied psychology and continued to shadow the acupuncturist. Immediately after my studies, I started working in the practice with the acupuncturist, finally also officially at the EUTCM. After each day of lessons, I could immediately put what I had learned into practice. A wonderful place to learn. So now I have been working with acupuncture for 46 years and have expanded the center into a place for integrative medicine. My strengths: reliable, human, analytical, and inventive",
