    "bio": "I was still a student in the physiotherapy program when I already knew that I wanted to study acupuncture. I think that my Chinese background has been an important factor. During the physiotherapy studies, this need became even stronger. The image of man that was used at that time in the Western medical world was too limited for me. Holistic thinking was a prerequisite for me to be able to practice well. Physiotherapist, Mensendieck exercise therapist, and acupuncturist. I have a lot of experience in guiding and treating people at all levels; from top athletes to severely disabled people. With my holistic approach, I complement the regular therapeutic view with attention to individual factors that influence physical and mental well-being. In 2016, I graduated from the Amsterdam University of Applied Sciences in the paramedical program of exercise therapy and physiotherapy. In 2020, I graduated in acupuncture at Qing-Bai (Traditional Chinese Medicine). In addition, I have done auriculotherapy (ear acupuncture). Furthermore, I have focused on the Balance Method according to Dr. Tan, the Yi Jing deepening course according to Dr. Chen Chao, and Wu Xing. In this way, I am able to apply the different techniques of Traditional Chinese Medicine in my treatment.",
