    "bio": "My name is Eriko. I come from Japan and completed my acupuncture training at the Meiji University for Integrative Medicine in Kyoto, which I graduated from in 2006. During my four-year study, I did internships at the university hospital where I worked in all departments. I gained further experience in various practices in Osaka where I worked on weekends and during holidays. After graduating, I worked full-time for three years - in Japan, that means six days a week - in an acupuncture practice in Osaka. There, I gained extensive experience in treating a wide range of complaints. In 2009, I moved to China to study Tai Chi and gain experience in the Chinese style of acupuncture. After a few years (in 2011), I temporarily left China to further my education in aromatherapy massage in London, as a complement to acupuncture. Upon returning to China, I had my own practice where I was able to help many people from around the world. In 2014, I moved to Heerenveen with my Dutch husband where I started Nagomi Japanese Acupuncture.",
