    "bio": "Roy works as an acupuncturist. He remembers a lecture at high school where someone talked more about acupuncture. He found it super interesting and this lecture has always stayed with him. After high school, he immersed himself in business administration and subsequently found his passion as an IT consultant. In 2011, colleague Els attended an open day of the Qing Bai acupuncture training and she was immediately enthusiastic. Roy actually wanted to know more about it as well, and at the open day he again tasted the flavor of wonder about all the possibilities with acupuncture. After four years of part-time training, Els started practice Acure in November 2015. Roy also treated occasionally but was mainly still engaged in IT work. Since 2018, Roy has fully come on board and thoroughly enjoys the amazing possibilities of acupuncture. Every day he sees the wonder in people. Pain they have been suffering from for years can usually be greatly reduced with the TAN method. Working with people, the privilege to be able to and allowed to stand so close to people, are gifts in themselves. Roy works with great pleasure and hopes to help as many people as possible with this wonderful healing method.",
