    "bio": "My name is Melroy and I have been an acupuncturist since 2017. I started in practice in 2013. First as a Qigong teacher, after which I started studying TuiNa. After that, acupuncture and then the Chinese herbal study again. There has always been a desire to practice a profession that could help people. What that entailed, I didn't know. Acupuncture actually came into my life and I adopted that lifestyle, with an emphasis on understanding Chinese medicine. And I still learn about it daily. Sometimes from the outside world, books, or social media, and sometimes from patients themselves. I work in a practice where we embrace holistic thinking and try to combine Eastern and Western approaches as much as possible. This way, we support people seeking help for their specific complaints in the broadest sense. Specializations change with the phases. We say: \"You get the patients that match your level at that moment\". In other words, we specialize in being all-round in the care that is required.",
