    "bio": "My name is Miriam Schoonderbeek and you are welcome at Praktijk de Branding for Acupuncture and Massage Therapy. During my work as a Massage Therapist, I came into contact with Traditional Chinese Medicine during the foot reflexology training. Once I had a taste, my interest was piqued and I couldn't let it go. I wanted to know and understand more. I pursued my studies at Academie Qing-Bai. It was clear to me from the start that I wanted to focus on women's health issues. I have since attended many further training sessions in areas such as menstrual disturbances, menopause, fertility issues, and vaginal complaints to deepen my understanding of women and gain as much knowledge as possible. In addition, I completed the Acupuncture & Oncology course at NVA. Acupuncture can be a wonderful complement to conventional treatment. A course of treatment can help reduce side effects and help to maintain balance as much as possible, both physically and mentally.",
