    "bio": "My name is Liesbeth van den Berg. In 1994 I started my career as a physiotherapist. Because I always feel that more knowledge can only improve my work, I also studied acupuncture alongside manual therapy. I started my acupuncture practice in 2006. Since January 1, 2018, I have also been working as an osteopath in my practice in Berlicum. I completed my osteopathy studies in 2016 with a Master of Science because I believe that we should also continue to look scientifically at the effectiveness and possibilities within the care we provide. This is to be able to provide care responsibly and more specifically. The goal of my practice is to shape integral healthcare by not only looking at the complaint but also searching further for the cause of your symptoms. An acupuncturist can often approach complaints that have been going on for years and even seemed unsolvable in a completely different way. This complementary form of healthcare is aimed at reducing complaints, increasing vitality, and balancing both body and mind. In addition, a scientific approach is aimed at your overall health.",
