    "bio": "How body and soul are connected to each other is something I find truly interesting. Often these are emotional and mental inhibiting patterns, alongside physical pain. Through further education about point names in acupuncture, I delved completely into their underlying meanings. That became my passion, passing on the ancient wisdom from the Tao where acupuncture has its foundation. By using point names, you can support your complaints. For example, Ren-4 Guān yuán (translated as the gate of origin) I use to bring you back to your own center if you are very sensitive. It's nice when people feel again that life flows, without being hindered by physical, emotional, or mental complaints. I believe that all diseases stem from a signal from the soul to bring you back to your center, your core. At least, that's how I've experienced it. This means that your pain is not there for nothing. My specializations are working with trauma, heightened sensitivity, and creative giftedness. Do you also want to discover what you can do with your complaints? You are most welcome.",
