    "bio": "As the daughter of an acupuncturist, I was introduced to Traditional Chinese Medicine at an early age and grew up with massage and acupuncture. Fascinated by the ancient methodology, the simplicity and at the same time the ingenuity of the meridian theory, I also made the transition to Traditional Chinese Medicine. In my practice, To the Point, I work with acupuncture, tuina massage, moxibustion, and cupping. In addition, I am a certified nutrition advisor; so I can give you advice on using food to promote your recovery and well-being. Every day I see and experience how healing and effective these techniques can be. Complaints that have sometimes been present for years can be resolved by simply and effectively 'switching on' the body by activating its so-called self-healing ability. But also early ailments can be effectively treated. Think of urinary tract infections, Frozen Shoulder, flu, etc. I aim for a pleasant, relaxing treatment that is effective but also provides insight into the complaints and how these complaints can be reduced. Each treatment is unique and tailored to the individual. Warm regards, Nicole Veenman",
    "education": [
      "Listed association: Nederlandse Vereniging voor Acupunctuur",
      "Source profile: acupunctuur.nl"
    ],
