    "bio": "My name is José Kleisen. In 1983 I started as a physiotherapist. Along the way, I realized that there must be an underlying cause if complaints do not go away. In 1994 I started the tuina training and a world opened up to me in the explanation of Traditional Chinese Medicine. I completed the training in 1996 and immediately switched to the acupuncture training. In 1998 I obtained my diploma and understood that there was still much to learn. That's why in 2000 I obtained the Stams and Branches and in 2002 the Chinese Herbal Medicine diploma. In 2007, a new world opened up again with the RADTS training. With that, I could further search for the cause. I now have a variety of possibilities to find the best way for clients in their recovery process. Gynecological complaints and allergies are the most common complaints in my practice, but due to my years of experience, there has never been a complaint where I wouldn't know what to do. My strength is that people feel understood and comfortable with me. I have a very good memory, not only for the complaints but also for what has been told to me in the past. Therefore, people do not have to keep telling everything again.",
