    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/12329/original/IMGP8006.JPG?1680531787",
    "bio": "My name is Saskia van der Schans-Toussaint. I am married and grew up in a family of general practitioners where both father and mother were general practitioners. It was instilled from an early age that a patient consists of more than just a complaint. This holistic approach has been a common thread in my work as a physiotherapist for over thirty years and found its place in the study of acupuncture. Since 2012, I have been working with great satisfaction in my acupuncture practice. The sometimes astonishing results continue to inspire me to further delve into Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) and to be able to work more tailor-made. Dr. Tan's Balance Method for pain complaints is an example of this. The search for solutions, for any problem, continues to fascinate me. The holistic aspect in TCM, where mental and physical activity are closely intertwined, combined with my work as a physiotherapist, provide me with a platform for an integrated treatment, where every person deserves 'the best of both worlds' .",
