    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/12184/original/afbeelding_profiel.jpg?1766048528",
    "bio": "'t Tij, practice for classical acupuncture Allow me to introduce myself: my name is Marleen Meijer-Lousberg. Since 1985, I have been working with great pleasure as a certified physiotherapist. During this time, I gained experience in a private practice (11 years) and in a nursing home (7 years). I also supervised pregnancy gymnastics and heart rehabilitation (3 years). After completing the four-year post-HBO acupuncture training at Nei Tsjing in Utrecht, I was able to start a practice for classical acupuncture. The 20th anniversary of the practice in 2018 was a grand day! I equally enjoy attending further training courses that meet the quality standards of the professional association. Some examples include: the four-year Medical Qi Gong training, a movement therapy that approaches the human being holistically and is a great addition to classical acupuncture; the annual Tuina and energetic massage training for acupuncturists, where I was able to incorporate these massage and mobilization techniques into my treatment options. The method is suitable for all ages, from babies to adults; my study trip to the TCM hospital in Qing Dao, China, a modern hospital specializing in Traditional Chinese Medicine, was a wonderful and educational experience. In addition to treatments, I enjoy giving lectures, internship supervision, and workshops on Medical Qi Gong upon request. The NVA is a professional organization of quality, of which I am a proud member. It guarantees the maintenance of quality and expert treatment. Regulations on ethics, hygiene, sterility, and further training ensure this quality. Pearl of Wisdom; 'Be like bamboo, bend with the wind and spring back, find your balance'.",
