    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/12498/original/Foto_Jos.jpg?1680531817",
    "bio": "My name is Jos van Vliet. I knew at a young age that I wanted to do something in complementary medicine (my father was a homeopath and radiesthetist). First, I thought I would look at regular care, so I became a nurse and later an ICU nurse. After nine years of hospital work and a year of traveling the world, in 1991 I started studying acupuncture/TCM. One of the most beautiful courses I have done. The Chinese way of thinking suited me perfectly. And after a year of practicing, I decided to do an internship in Beijing. A fantastic experience. Since 1994, I had a half-time job in intensive care and a half-time job as an acupuncturist. I stopped working in regular care in 2002. In 1998, I also followed the training to become a mesologist (which, among other things, uses the electrophysiology of acupuncture points according to Dr. Voll). I now have a full-time practice in acupuncture and mesology (a protected profession) in Nijmegen. The Chinese way of thinking is now in my genes. I also use the latest measurement techniques with the Oberon and Human from Metavitall. In these, the acupuncture measurement points are measured according to Voll's electro-acupuncture. In addition, the entire body is fully scanned using biophoton technology, and you can see on the screen where the dysfunctions and disturbances in your system are located. A huge addition to my acupuncture practice. I invite you for a free introductory phone call!",
