    "bio": "Hello, I am Margot Arnts, an experienced physiotherapist and manual therapist, and I have specialized in a holistic approach to healthcare. After many years of working in physiotherapy and manual therapy, I decided to expand my knowledge and skills to the world of acupuncture. During this study, I learned even more about the value of seeing the whole person. In order to unravel the underlying cause of a pattern of complaints and to be able to help clients at a deeper level so that you can remain free of complaints in the long term. After graduating in 2023, I founded Qi-Care Practice for Acupuncture and since July 2024, I have had the pleasure of conducting my acupuncture practice within the Plato general practice. My vision I believe that the body has a powerful ability to heal itself and I see acupuncture as a means to activate that inner strength. With personal attention and care, I tailor each treatment to the unique needs of my clients, so that they feel stronger and more balanced both physically and mentally. My goal is to provide a peaceful environment where you can work on your health and well-being with complete confidence.",
