    "image": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/assets1.acupunctuur.nl/profiles/12729/original/IMG_0018.jpg?1721046991",
    "bio": "My passion for practicing Chinese medicine is rooted in the core principle that in life and health everything is interconnected. The powerful and holistic approach that Chinese medicine offers for health and well-being greatly motivates me. I enjoy applying my knowledge and experience to help people restore and maintain their physical, mental, and emotional balance. My practice is a comfortable and safe environment where I combine East Asian healing methods and philosophies with science, mindfulness, and breathing exercises. This allows me to offer personalized treatments for a wide range of complaints. My treatments are individually tailored based on a comprehensive diagnosis. This enables me to adjust the treatment optimally to someone's constitution, needs, and health complaints. I have a proven track record in diagnosing and developing successful treatments that combine the aforementioned practices. This approach is applicable to a wide range of health issues. In addition to treatment and to improve overall health, I also offer personalized lifestyle advice (nutrition, exercise, stress management, sleep habits, etc.). I specialize in evaluating patients from the perspective of Chinese medicine. Additionally, I can also assess disease characteristics from a Western medical perspective. If necessary, I refer patients to a specialist. I graduated with 'First-Class Honours' in Chinese medicine from the University of Westminster in London. During my studies, the focus was on acupuncture, tui na (Chinese massage therapy), cupping, moxibustion, gua sha, and nutrition and lifestyle advice according to Chinese medicine. I also obtained my qualification as a tui na therapist at The City College of Acupuncture London. I regularly attend courses and events to ensure my continuous professional development. This allows me to stay informed about the latest research and treatment methods and continuously improve my skills as a practitioner of Chinese medicine for the benefit of my patients. Note: The language used on my website is English.",
